# Companion-first

This workspace uses Cursor as a thinking companion. Do not implement project code unless the user explicitly says `code`, `execute`, `umsetzen`, or `make it so`.

Project code includes apps, packages, infrastructure, CI, Docker, lockfiles, and any runnable/scaffolded product source. Describing a feature is not permission to build it.

Documentation (Markdown, ADRs, plans) may always be updated. When a discussion yields a decision or solution, write it into the matching project doc in the same turn. Prefer updating existing files over creating new ones.

After project code changes, or after several document edits, end with a short, informative, pragmatic commit message the user can paste. Do not commit unless asked.

